# Meizu M6 (mtk-kpd) keylayout
# Android input device "mtk-kpd": bus=0x0019 vendor=0x2454 product=0x6500
# EventHub resolves Vendor_2454_Product_6500.kl BEFORE Generic.kl, so this
# overrides the stock fallback that mapped scancode 102 -> MOVE_HOME
# (the "scroll to top of list" behavior reported on the capacitive Home button).
#
# Ground truth (live, device 711HEBSR277K5):
#   - mtk-kpd (event1) advertises only scancodes 102,114,115,116,129,193,408
#     (from /proc/bus/input/devices KEY bitmap). It can physically emit 102.
#   - Before fix dumpsys input showed KeyLayoutFile=/system/usr/keylayout/Generic.kl
#     and Generic.kl:124 "key 102 MOVE_HOME".
#   - After placing this file + reboot, dumpsys input shows
#     KeyLayoutFile=/system/usr/keylayout/Vendor_2454_Product_6500.kl and
#     injecting scancode 102 on event1 sends the device Home (Settings->launcher).
#
# Install: push to /system/usr/keylayout/ (chmod 644, restorecon), survives reboot.

key 102   HOME
key 158   BACK
key 139   MENU
key 129   MENU
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
key 115   VOLUME_UP
key 116   POWER
